# samples/user/voice: takes licensed from GameDevMarket under its Marketplace Terms, Licence (A). 4.1 allows using and
# adapting them inside a media product without limit; 4.2(b) forbids sharing or redistributing the asset other than as
# part of that product, and a public git repo is exactly that. The pack stays on the machine that licensed it, so
# songs/hunted.strudel checks and plays here and reports a missing pack anywhere else.
samples/user/voice/
.playwright-mcp/
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
!.claude/skills/strudel/
/docs
dist/
renders/
*.bak

# test fixtures: the suite writes _t_-prefixed files into test/, songs/ and samples/user/ and deletes them after; an interrupted run leaves them, and they are never to be committed
_t_*
